WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.886
ALEX: So for anyone building or
buying enterprise AI

00:00:01.886 --> 00:00:03.771
ALEX: right now — what do you do
with

00:00:03.771 --> 00:00:05.657
ALEX: this?

00:00:05.742 --> 00:00:08.519
RUFUS: You use it as a benchmark.
Whatever agent

00:00:08.519 --> 00:00:11.297
RUFUS: security tooling you're
currently running — software
guardrails,

00:00:11.297 --> 00:00:14.074
RUFUS: observability platforms —
you now have a hardware-enforced

00:00:14.074 --> 00:00:16.851
RUFUS: option to measure against.

00:00:16.961 --> 00:00:19.316
JAMIE: And if you're in a
regulated industry —

00:00:19.316 --> 00:00:21.670
JAMIE: finance, healthcare,
defense — the millisecond
quarantine claim

00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:24.025
JAMIE: is worth testing seriously,
because an agent acting

00:00:24.025 --> 00:00:26.379
JAMIE: outside its bounds in those
environments is not

00:00:26.379 --> 00:00:28.734
JAMIE: a theoretical cost.

00:00:28.914 --> 00:00:31.572
ALEX: NVIDIA says the capacity
gain is "up to"

00:00:31.572 --> 00:00:34.231
ALEX: 20%, which is a ceiling, not
a floor.
